# ============================================================================
# CineOps Guardian — what ships to GitHub
#
# Rule of thumb: the repo contains the product (engine/, src/cineops/, the
# chassis it composes, contracts, config, corpus, docs, deck, deploy scripts)
# plus the delivery evidence a judge needs to re-run it. Everything produced
# by the local build/agent harness while BUILDING it stays out.
# NOTE: git does not support trailing comments on a pattern line — every
# comment here is on its own line.
# ============================================================================

# --- Credentials (generic patterns only; never project-specific) ------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.e2e.example
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
credentials*.json
*credentials.json
secrets*.json
.aws/
.gcp/
.azure/
*service-account*.json

# --- Chassis / tooling caches -----------------------------------------------
.cache/
/examples/
.DS_Store

# ============================================================================
# run_sweep.sh engine-building harness
# Everything the sweep driver reads/writes while implementing the engine. None
# of it is product; all of it is machine-local run state. Derived from
# run_sweep.sh variables: CONTROL_DIR (.control), MSG_DIR (.intramessages),
# PI_SESSION_DIR (.pi_sessions), CHAT_DIR (.chat), SUMMARY_DIR (.run_summaries),
# SUPERVISOR_DIR (.supervisor), LOCK_DIR (.run_sweep.lock), STATE_FILE
# (run_state.json), STEP_RECORDS_FILE, SID_LIST_FILE (.step_sids.tmp),
# LOG_FILE (.sequential_run.log), RESULTS_FILE, PLANNER_LOG_FILE,
# PLANNER_RESULTS_FILE, DEBUG_FILE (.debug_run.log), FLIGHT_FILE
# (.prompt_flight.md), STATUS_REPORT_FILE, HANDOVER_FILE (handout.md),
# DRIVER_LOG (_driver.log), PLANNER_CONF (run_planner.conf), SEQMD_CONF
# (run_sequential_md.conf), ROLE_FILE (models.json), PROMPTS_FILE, plus the
# generated prompt sets under .run_sweep/ and the driver stdout transcripts.
# ============================================================================
.chat/
.run_sweep/
.run_sweep.lock/
.control/
.intramessages/
.pi_sessions/
.supervisor/
.run_summaries/
.run_step_records.txt
.step_sids.tmp
.sequential_run.log
.sequential_results.txt
.planner_run.log
.planner_results.txt
.debug_run.log
.prompt_flight.md
status_report.md
handout.md
handout_active.md
run_state.json
run_planner.conf
run_sequential_md.conf
models.json
prompts.json
_driver.log
_run.log
_handout.log
_chunk_*.md
# The driver script itself: it is the build harness (and names non-Google
# coding-assistant models in its role file), not the entry. Delete this line
# if you decide to publish it.
run_sweep.sh

# --- E2E delivery-gate scratch (probe logs, downloaded binaries) -------------
.e2e-*.log
.e2e-*.err
.e2e-bin/
# Regenerated by `bash scripts/hygiene.sh` on every run; the gate is the
# script, not a checked-in snapshot of its output.
hygiene-report.json
hygiene-report.md

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# --- Node / build -------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.next/
out/
/tmp/

# ============================================================================
# Authoring docs — local planning material, not part of the product.
# Two deliberate exceptions: design_documents/e2e-testing/ is delivery evidence
# (the testing strategy + the runnable Playwright suite a judge can
# re-execute). Its heavy run output and operator secrets still stay out.
# design_documents/tutorial/ is the end-to-end walkthrough for running the app.
# ============================================================================
design_documents/*
!design_documents/e2e-testing/
!design_documents/tutorial/
# Superseded drafts the owner has parked (their `ignore_` prefix).
design_documents/tutorial/ignore_*
design_documents/e2e-testing/playwright-report/
design_documents/e2e-testing/test-results/
design_documents/e2e-testing/telemetry/.work/
/templates/
/private/
/demo/
/deck/
script.md

